base('chain-rule','The multivariable chain rule',['u and the curve γ are continuously differentiable on the relevant domain.'],'d/dt u(t,γ(t))=u_t(t,γ(t))+∇u(t,γ(t))·γ′(t).','This is an accepted calculus theorem at the current boundary. A proof proceeds from differentiability’s linear approximation and a remainder tending to zero. That remainder proof is not expanded here.','Standard theorem boundary')
