base('product-rule','Product and exponential differentiation',['f,g are differentiable, and C is constant.'],'(fg)′=f′g+fg′ and (e^(−Ct))′=−Ce^(−Ct).','These standard calculus rules are accepted here. The product rule comes from a difference-quotient expansion; the exponential rule also requires the derivative of the exponential.','Standard theorem boundary')
