add('weighted-energy','Remove exponential growth by a weight',['E is differentiable and E′≤CE; C is constant.'],'F=e^(−Ct)E has F′≤0.','Product differentiation gives F′=e^(−Ct)(E′−CE). The assumed inequality makes the bracket nonpositive; the exponential is positive, so multiplying preserves its sign.',['product-rule'])
